  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05IY">Definition <span data-tag="05IY">38.15.2</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/05FW" data-tag="05FW">38.15.1</a> we say a diagram (<a href="/tag/05IX" data-tag="05IX">38.15.1.1</a>) defines an <em>impurity of $\mathcal{F}$ above $s$</em> if $\xi \in \text{Ass}_{X_ T/T}(\mathcal{F}_ T)$ and $\overline{\{ \xi \} } \cap X_ t = \emptyset $. We will indicate this by saying “let $(g : T \to S, t' \leadsto t, \xi )$ be an impurity of $\mathcal{F}$ above $s$”. </p>
